1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:01,220
What Is True Faith?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,300
Introduction: Christ as the Foundation, Faith as Our Living Response

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:13,160
In hardship and waiting, we often hope God will change our circumstances

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:17,120
and answer our prayers in the way we desire.

5
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:23,560
Yet health, family relationships, or work may not improve, even after earnest

6
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:29,800
prayer. The foundation of Christian life is Jesus Christ, not the strength of our

7
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:36,240
believing. Faith is our reliance on Him: receiving and responding to the grace God
has

8
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:41,420
freely given in Christ, rather than trying to make God do what we want.

9
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:48,400
The life of faith is not an exercise in self-motivation, nor does it require

10
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,920
us to make reality sound better than it is.

11
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:57,080
Biblical faith does not avoid the complexity of human life.

12
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:01,760
We experience weakness and pain, and we have questions.

13
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:06,980
Faith does not ask us to convince ourselves that we are invincible.

14
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:13,200
It invites us to turn toward the trustworthy God while much remains unexplained.

15
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:19,420
Admitting that we do not know is not the same as denying His faithfulness.

16
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:26,620
True faith is not believing that God will always do what we want, but trusting that
He

17
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,240
remains faithful even when He does not.

18
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:35,720
We may tell God what we hope for and acknowledge how difficult waiting has
become.

19
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:39,940
Trusting Him does not mean that we always feel secure.

20
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:46,120
It means entrusting our lives to the Lord of grace even in confusion and weakness.

21
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:51,200
Faith and Reason: Trust Beyond What We See, Not a Leap in the Dark

22
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:56,120
Now faith is assurance of things hoped for, proof of things not seen.

23
00:01:56,560 --> 00:02:00,620
— Hebrews 11:1 (WEB)

24
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:07,660
Faith is assurance concerning what we hope for and confidence concerning what we
do not

25
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:13,820
yet see. It rests on God and His promises, not on our changing feelings.

26
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:19,760
Hebrews 11:3 directs our understanding of creation toward God’s word;

27
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:25,060
it does not ask us to substitute faith for every form of inquiry.

28
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:31,400
Learning the facts, receiving appropriate medical care, seeking reliable advice, and

29
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,280
planning thoughtfully need not conflict with trust in God.

30
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:42,120
We can ask honest questions while acknowledging that our understanding remains
limited.

31
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:46,320
We do not create reality through the force of belief.

32
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:50,600
We trust the God who created and sustains all things.

33
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:56,940
His faithfulness does not rise and fall with our emotions, and His promises are not

34
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:00,680
identical to the outcomes we have chosen for ourselves.

35
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:06,880
When the road ahead remains unclear, faith keeps us listening to His word,
discerning

36
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:11,020
the next step, and responding with hope and obedience.

37
00:03:11,380 --> 00:03:16,120
The Faith of Abel and Enoch: God’s Commendation and Diverse Outcomes

38
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:23,520
Genesis 4:3–5 recounts Cain and Abel bringing offerings and God’s regard for Abel
and

39
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:29,640
his offering. Hebrews 11:4 explains that Abel offered a more excellent sacrifice

40
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:33,760
by faith and received testimony that he was righteous.

41
00:03:34,340 --> 00:03:38,080
The explanation in terms of faith comes from Hebrews.

42
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:44,200
We should neither invent Abel’s unrecorded motives nor insist that differences
between

43
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:46,300
the offerings had no significance.

44
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:52,520
Enoch’s walk with God is recorded in Genesis 5:22 and 24.

45
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:59,060
Hebrews 11:5 emphasizes that he was taken up by faith and had already

46
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:03,280
received testimony of God’s pleasure before he was taken.

47
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:07,320
Abel died, while Enoch did not experience death.

48
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:14,000
Scripture does not use these different outcomes to rank their faith, nor does it
promise

49
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,820
that every believer will escape death.

50
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:23,880
Neither outcome gives us a scale for measuring faith by present circumstances.

51
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:30,920
Without faith it is impossible to be well pleasing to him, for he who comes to God
must

52
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:37,040
believe that he exists, and that he is a rewarder of those who seek him.

53
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:39,380
— Hebrews 11:6 (WEB)

54
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:46,200
God commends faith because it trusts Him, not because it has mastered a religious

55
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:52,160
technique. Hebrews 11:6 speaks of the God who exists and

56
00:04:52,160 --> 00:04:54,260
rewards those who seek Him.

57
00:04:54,700 --> 00:05:01,120
Read alongside Hebrews 11:13–16 and 35–40, that reward cannot be

58
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:05,820
reduced to wealth, health, or favorable circumstances in this life.

59
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:12,000
It directs our attention beyond immediate gains and losses toward God’s promises
and the

60
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,980
better country. Fellowship with God, new life, and eternal hope help us understand
that

61
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:21,600
reward within the letter’s wider message;

62
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:26,100
they are not bargaining terms with which to secure the outcome we want.

63
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:30,860
Faith and Grace: Wesleyan Theology on the Journey of Sanctification

64
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:37,760
The Wesleyan tradition understands salvation, from beginning to end, as the work
of

65
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:44,100
God’s grace. Prevenient grace comes before our response, awakening us and

66
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:47,260
enabling us to respond to the gospel.

67
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:53,500
Justification by faith means receiving forgiveness in Christ and being reconciled to

68
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:57,140
God, rather than accumulating merit through works.

69
00:05:57,940 --> 00:06:03,320
Sanctification is the Holy Spirit’s continuing work of renewing our lives so that we

70
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:05,640
grow in love for God and neighbor.

71
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:10,700
Justification and sanctification belong together, but they are not interchangeable.

72
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:15,800
Obedience, then, is not the price we pay for salvation;

73
00:06:15,820 --> 00:06:19,300
it is the response of a life that trusts God.

74
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:25,740
Receiving salvation freely does not excuse us from repentance or love for others.

75
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:32,520
Grace enables our response and calls for a response expressed in action.

76
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:39,360
As the Spirit renews us, gratitude begins to shape how we treat people, carry out

77
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:43,540
our responsibilities, and respond to temptation.

78
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:48,560
We do not have to make ourselves perfect before we are permitted to approach God.

79
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:54,640
We draw near because of Christ’s saving work, and within His grace we learn
obedience

80
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:58,040
and responsibility. Growth takes time.

81
00:06:58,260 --> 00:07:03,520
The presence of weakness is not a reason to stop seeking help or to give up
responding

82
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,380
to God.

83
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:08,080
Faith Amid Suffering: Weakness, Community, and Authentic Hope

84
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:15,620
Hebrews 10:32–39 reminds its readers of the suffering and losses they had

85
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:18,540
endured and urges them to persevere.

86
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:25,140
Hebrews 11:13 and 35–40 also shows that some died without seeing the complete

87
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:27,020
fulfillment of the promises.

88
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:32,280
True faith makes room for weakness, confusion, and the strain of waiting.

89
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:38,460
We need not pretend to feel strong at all times, nor claim to know the reason for
every

90
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:43,800
instance of suffering. Coming to God in tears to seek mercy is not the opposite of

91
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,260
faith.

92
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:50,600
Faith is not a lonely struggle, but a life in which we help one another through

93
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:56,800
hardship. Hebrews 10:24–25 urges believers to consider one

94
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:01,520
another, encourage love and good works, and value meeting together.

95
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:06,660
The church’s companionship, encouragement, and prayer matter deeply.

96
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:13,260
This does not mean that someone temporarily unable to gather has been
abandoned by God.

97
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:20,000
We should seek practical ways to care for one another within our circumstances,
rather

98
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,540
than place another barrier before those who are already struggling.

99
00:08:24,862 --> 00:08:29,262
Imagine someone who has unexpectedly lost a job.

100
00:08:29,262 --> 00:08:33,362
After weeks of prayer, there is still no offer of work.

101
00:08:34,242 --> 00:08:39,142
Faith does not require this person to pretend to be unconcerned.

102
00:08:39,502 --> 00:08:45,842
It makes room to bring real needs honestly before God and to ask trusted people in
the

103
00:08:45,842 --> 00:08:51,902
church for help. Alongside prayer, Scripture, and wise advice, there are

104
00:08:51,902 --> 00:08:58,382
practical steps to take: pursuing work, managing household expenses, and making
honest

105
00:08:58,382 --> 00:09:04,762
decisions. Circumstances may not change immediately, but the burden need not be
carried

106
00:09:04,762 --> 00:09:10,582
alone. Concealing fear is not a requirement for proving that one has faith.

107
00:09:10,582 --> 00:09:15,802
Conclusion: Fixing Our Eyes on Christ, Looking Toward a Better Country

108
00:09:16,902 --> 00:09:21,802
Our final reliance is on Christ, not on our own endurance.

109
00:09:22,902 --> 00:09:28,982
Hebrews 9:28 speaks of His being offered once to bear the sins of many;

110
00:09:29,142 --> 00:09:35,382
Hebrews 4:15–16 speaks of His sympathy with our weaknesses and our freedom

111
00:09:35,382 --> 00:09:40,502
to seek mercy and grace. Bearing sin concerns His saving work;

112
00:09:40,602 --> 00:09:44,162
sympathizing with weakness speaks of His understanding and help.

113
00:09:44,842 --> 00:09:47,942
We should not collapse these into a single expression.

114
00:09:48,502 --> 00:09:54,182
The better country of Hebrews 11:16 is heavenly, a hope God has prepared for His

115
00:09:54,182 --> 00:10:00,202
people. Looking toward it does not make our responsibilities today unimportant.

116
00:10:00,702 --> 00:10:06,442
looking to Jesus, the author and perfecter of faith, who for the joy that was set
before

117
00:10:06,442 --> 00:10:11,762
him endured the cross, despising its shame, and has sat down at the right hand of
the

118
00:10:11,762 --> 00:10:12,602
throne of God.

119
00:10:13,162 --> 00:10:14,882
— Hebrews 12:2 (WEB)

120
00:10:15,842 --> 00:10:21,962
Faith does not deny the pain of reality or demand that we become strong overnight.

121
00:10:22,662 --> 00:10:28,582
In prayer, patient endurance, and practical action, we keep looking to the Lord who

122
00:10:28,582 --> 00:10:32,382
endured the cross and now sits at God’s right hand.

123
00:10:33,162 --> 00:10:35,162
Questions may remain unanswered.

124
00:10:35,162 --> 00:10:40,902
Even so, we can walk together in hope, looking forward to the day when we will see
Him.
